<%# A message's featured button (Chats::Action): the one place it takes you,
    under the words it came with. Rendered inside the bubble, so it is part
    of the single viewer-agnostic broadcast render AND of the clone the
    long-press popup lifts — which is why it is a plain link and never a
    form: a form would need a per-viewer CSRF token baked into a render
    every subscriber shares. An action is a destination, not a mutation.

    data-turbo-frame="_top": older pages of a thread arrive inside lazy
    `chats_page_…` turbo-frames, and a link inside a frame navigates the
    FRAME. _top makes it navigate the page, wherever the bubble landed.

    The url was validated at the write (Chats::Message#
    action_must_be_well_formed): http(s) or a path on this site, never
    `javascript:` or protocol-relative. %>
<%= link_to action.label, action.url, class: "chats-message__action", data: { turbo_frame: "_top" } %>
